+# Team Decisions
+
+## Search swaps the members panel; an invite answers the page
+**Date:** 30. 09. 26
+**Context:** The search box must filter without a reload, and a successful invite must show the new member and reset the form, also without a reload.
+**Decision:** The search box lives inside the members panel (`teamIds.membersPanel`), and `GET /team/members` answers that panel as a fragment. `POST /team` answers the whole page on success (`.submit` morphs `#main-content`) and the invite form region alone on a 422 (`{ invalid: teamIds.inviteForm }`). The invite form carries `.behavior("resetOnSuccess")`.
+**Reasoning:** htmx 4's morph copies an input's live value only when its `value` attribute changes, so a success morph alone leaves typed text in place. `resetOnSuccess` clears the invite form. The search box renders its query as a `value` attribute on every panel render, so the success page (empty query) clears it and the box never disagrees with the unfiltered list that now shows the new member.
+**Consequences:** A successful invite clears any active search. The search input is re-rendered by its own swap; the morph keeps focus and the caret because the node keeps its id.
+
+## Invite validation is server-only
+**Date:** 30. 09. 26
+**Context:** Native `required`/`type=email` checks would pre-empt the server's messages for two of the three rules, leaving the duplicate-email rule as the only inline message.
+**Decision:** The invite form sets `novalidate` (htmx 4 honours `form.noValidate`), and the service validates every rule, answering a 422 with per-field messages.
+**Reasoning:** One validation voice, rendered next to the fields the way the spec asks.
+**Consequences:** Controls keep `required` for assistive tech; the browser never blocks the submit.
