+# Team page
+
+## Problem
+Signed-in users have no place to see who is on their team or to add someone to it.
+
+## Appetite
+Small batch: one feature module, no schema changes.
+
+## Solution
+- `/team`, guarded: the team's members (name, email, role, status badge).
+- A search box above the list narrows it by name or email as the user types (HTMX fragment swap, no reload).
+- An "Invite member" form (name, email, role) adds an invited member. Server-side validation: name required, email valid and not already on the team; errors render next to their fields with the typed values kept.
+- Empty team: an empty state prompting an invite. Search with no hits: says so and names the query.
+- Main navigation links to it.
+
+## Rabbit Holes
+- Keeping the search box and the list consistent after an invite (see [decisions.md](decisions.md)).
+
+## No-Gos
+- No database: members live in an in-memory store inside the feature, seeded with three members, reset on restart.
+- No invitation emails, no accept flow, no editing or removing members, no per-team permissions.
